Why This Market Matters
Bidirectional DC power supplies provide an efficient platform for testing systems in which energy must move repeatedly between a source and a device under test. This capability is particularly valuable for high-capacity batteries, EV powertrains, chargers, inverters, fuel cells, and energy-storage systems. Regenerative operation can reduce electricity losses and cooling requirements compared with conventional resistive loading. As vehicle voltage levels and battery capacities increase, demand for scalable high-power testing equipment is expanding. Software automation and wide-bandgap semiconductor technologies are also becoming increasingly important differentiators.

